  "salt": "eNksJ2UtQZmRGLn7YO48OA==",
  "text": "Cormac mac Airt is the greatest of the Cormacs of Ireland. He ruled Tara, and the land prospered under his right rule. Salmon leapt from the rivers, the fields stood heavy with grain, and the cows gave more milk than the pails could hold. The warrior FIONN MAC CUMHAILL led the FIANNA in Cormac time. Signs marked his birth, for his father Art mac Cuinn heard a smith prophecy that a child by his daughter ACHTAN would become king. Achtan bore Cormac in a thunderstorm beneath a hedgerow, and a wolf suckled the babe. As king he visited the Otherworld and came back with a golden cup that broke when a lie was told and mended at the truth. He lost the throne after his son raped a king daughter; a fight put out his eye, and a blemished king could not rule. He stepped aside for his son Cairbre Lifechair.",
